WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.680
A principle can state a standard connecting a kind of case to a judgment, permission or obligation.

2
00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.841
Applying it means matching the case to the standard’s complete conditions.

3
00:00:11.141 --> 00:00:15.216
A study using identifiable records requires ethics review.

4
00:00:15.516 --> 00:00:18.311
Study T uses identifiable records.

5
00:00:18.611 --> 00:00:23.560
The study meets the condition stated by the principle, so the review requirement applies.

6
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.335
The argument has not said the review occurred.

7
00:00:26.635 --> 00:00:33.419
If a candidate conclusion instead said T was already reviewed, it would substitute compliance for the requirement.

8
00:00:33.719 --> 00:00:37.623
That change matters even though the words ethics review appear in both.

9
00:00:37.923 --> 00:00:43.299
Principle questions often use familiar conditional structure with different kinds of results.

10
00:00:43.599 --> 00:00:47.097
Keep both the factual fit and the judgment’s strength accurate.

11
00:00:47.397 --> 00:00:51.216
List the relevant case facts without adding missing qualifications.

12
00:00:51.516 --> 00:00:54.417
A standard requiring two conditions needs both.

13
00:00:54.717 --> 00:00:58.984
Say the case and the standard in ordinary language before matching them.

14
00:00:59.284 --> 00:01:07.604
A shared moral topic does not establish the conditional fit, and a familiar result cannot stand in for an unproved prerequisite.
